.9%, so growth at these returns destroys value.","It converts 13% of revenue into free cash flow, or 10% after stock compensation.","ROE of 42% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (1.4x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 12pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 4.5% of revenue on R&D and 3.5% on stock compensation (above the 2% gate)."],"hlth":["The balance sheet carries net cash of $171.4M (17% of market cap).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 2.94)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 19.7% over 3 years and 14.8% over 5 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 32%).","Free cash flow has compounded 67.5% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+2.4% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue down 6%.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.3x, 0.7% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 24, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own 13.0%, meaningful skin in the game, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Insiders have only sold over the past year (15 sales, net $1.6M sold).","It returns 2.1% a year to shareholders (2.1% in buybacks).","Short interest is elevated at 28.1% of the float, 7.5 days to cover."],"people":["With about 356 employees, each generates about $1.9M of revenue, 3.2x the Communication Services median, and productivity has risen 22.9% a year.","That works out to $254K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.4M (1x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $68K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":67,"head":"Watch: ROIC 30.9% vs WACC 9.9%.","pros":["Trades 19% below fair value of $35.48","FCF margin 13.0%","Revenue grew 14.8%/yr over 5y","Net cash of $171.4M","Altman Z in the safe zone"],"cons":["ROIC 30.9% vs WACC 9.9%","12-1 month momentum -22%"],"flag